# A transitively imported module — ouroboros#141 arm A.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that the collision guard compared the PROGRAM
# against the modules the program imported; a module imported by a module was
# never compared against anything, so its bindings merged into the spliced
# scope unguarded. Here three files bind `ctr` — the program (1), _arm_outer
# (50) and _arm_inner (7) — and each must keep its own.
#
# The renamer is applied recursively: _arm_inner is spliced under
# `_arm_inner__`, _arm_outer under `_arm_outer__`, and _arm_outer's own
# `import _arm_inner` binds `_arm_outer___arm_inner` to the SAME dict object
# the program would get from `import _arm_inner` (the VM's module cache).
# `keys of _arm_outer` does NOT carry `_arm_inner`: an import is a top-level
# binding of the importing module, but a `_`-prefixed binding is omitted from
# the module dict (#142) — which is why the dict-chain read lives in t311,
# whose links have public names. Here the chain is reached through FUNCTIONS
# only, the road the old guard left unchecked.
ctr is 1
import _arm_outer
print of (_arm_outer.via of null)
print of (_arm_outer.mine of null)
print of ctr
print of (keys of _arm_outer)
print of _arm_outer.ctr
